      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update airflow to 3.3.2-5 or later.",
      "status_notes": "GHSA-5639-2j2p-m4mx (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5639-2j2p-m4mx) affects Mako 1.4.1 and earlier and is fixed in Mako 1.4.2 by upstream commit https://github.com/sqlalchemy/mako/commit/000ed85e4e48771eff460bf4fc721fb43de80e08 (\"Fix path traversal via drive designator URI on Windows in TemplateLookup\"), which is in the rel_1_4_2 tag but not in rel_1_4_1. The issue concerns drive-letter URIs on Windows; this decision records the first build that ships the upstream fix rather than resting on the platform. The file list of every published airflow build on amd64 and arm64 (3.3.0-0 through 3.4.0-7) carries Mako under usr/lib/airflow/lib/python3.13/site-packages at these versions: 1.3.12 in 3.3.0-0 through 3.3.0-3, 1.4.1 in 3.3.1-0 through 3.3.2-4, 1.4.2 in 3.3.2-5 through 3.3.2-14, and 1.4.3 in 3.3.2-15 through the current 3.4.0-7. 3.3.2-5 is the first build with Mako 1.4.2 or later, and under Debian version ordering every build below it carries an affected release and every build from it on carries a fixed one."
